    "reason": "The whitelist and selected readers apply only to changed native schemas. Legacy-equal schemas return before restoration. Native scans preserve restored same-generation parent keys and use the existing publication snapshot facts. Court extraction uses the existing exact witnessed-prior comparison before resolving the original recorded opinion parent. Original legacy dimension readers, bindings, cached validation, and end-of-build checks are unchanged. Native readers retain their per-table implementation identities. Current bulk and regulatory subjects use the same selected receipt restoration. Native rulemaking snapshots bind their actual pointer, immutable manifest and declared subject/receipt bytes and generation; their native schema and original processing facts use the maintained reader. Without native receipts, the original census entries and input fingerprints remain identical. Immutable native snapshot pins replace mutable-export ETag checks only for that new path. The documents restoration allowance is finite and scoped to that dataset. Selected documents and Register native scans queue sequentially before their per-scan timer starts; other scans retain parallelism. Cache acceptance, values, source bindings and measurement functions remain unchanged.",
